    "id": "c15",
    "paper": "GE",
    "unit": "2",
    "unitTitle": "Letter Writing",
    "sub": "A worked official letter, start to finish",
    "def": "A complete specimen: a plausible prompt, the letter laid out correctly, and a note on why each part sits where it does. Format is learnt by seeing one done, not by reading about it.",
    "exp": "THE PROMPT\n\nYou are the System Manager, Mizoram Urban Development Agency Ltd., Aizawl. Write to the Deputy Commissioner, Aizawl District, requesting allotment of a room in the District Complex to house the Agency's server equipment, referring to a discussion held earlier.\n\nTHE LETTER\n\nFrom:\nThe System Manager,\nMizoram Urban Development Agency Ltd.,\nAizawl - 796001\n\nNo. MUDAL/IT/2026/47\nDated Aizawl, the 28th August, 2026\n\nTo:\nThe Deputy Commissioner,\nAizawl District,\nAizawl - 796001\n\nSubject: Request for allotment of a room in the District Complex for installation of server equipment\n\nReference: Discussion held in your office on the 12th August, 2026\n\nSir,\n\nWith reference to the discussion cited above, I am directed to request the allotment of one room of approximately 200 square feet in the District Complex for the installation of server and networking equipment of this Agency.\n\nThe Agency proposes to shift its server from the present rented premises, where the power supply is unstable and the room cannot be secured after office hours. A room on the ground floor with an independent electrical connection would be suitable. The Agency will meet the cost of air-conditioning and access control.\n\nIt is therefore requested that the allotment may kindly be sanctioned at an early date, so that the shifting may be completed before the close of the current financial year.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n(A. Lalthanga)\nSystem Manager\nMizoram Urban Development Agency Ltd.\n\nEncl.: 1. Layout plan of the proposed room\n       2. Estimate of installation cost\n\nCopy to: The Managing Director, MUDAL, for information.\n\nWHY EACH PART SITS WHERE IT DOES\n\nThe sender's block and the letter number come first because the file is identified before the content. The subject follows the addressee so a clerk can route the letter without reading the body, and it is a noun phrase. The reference cites the earlier discussion, which is why the body can open with 'With reference to the discussion cited above' instead of re-narrating it.\n\n'Sir' pairs with 'Yours faithfully' because the letter is addressed to a designation, not a named person. The body runs opening, substance, action sought - and the request is restated explicitly in the closing paragraph so the reader cannot finish unsure what is wanted. The signature block carries the designation, because the office signs, not the individual. Both enclosures are named in the body and listed below.",
    "facts": [
      "The subject line follows the addressee's address and precedes the salutation",
      "'Sir' pairs with 'Yours faithfully' because the addressee is a designation",
      "The reference line lets the body open without re-narrating earlier correspondence",
      "The action sought is restated in the closing paragraph of the body",
      "Enclosures named in the body are listed after the signature block"
    ],
    "traps": [
      "Placing the subject line above the addressee's address",
      "Closing 'Yours sincerely' after 'Sir'",
      "Signing without the designation, which makes an official letter read as a personal one",
      "Leaving the request implied by the narrative instead of stating it in the close"
    ],
    "mnem": "",
    "rel": [
      "The parts of an official letter",
      "Subject line, reference and enclosures",
      "Salutations and subscriptions"
    ],
    "derived": true,
    "prov": "The official syllabus lists this General English component with its marks only and enumerates no subtopics. This breakdown is derived, not official."
